Campfire for BEAM: wallet-api and beam-node listen on 127.0.0.1 only.

wallet-api: bind the API server to loopback (stock binds 0.0.0.0; --ip_whitelist
closes a socket only after accept, so the port is still reachable on the LAN).

beam-node: bind the P2P listener to loopback, turn off the UDP LAN beacon (it binds
0.0.0.0 and advertises the listen port), and do not send PeerInfoSelf while listening
on loopback, so remote peers do not record and gossip this host as a reachable node.
Outbound connections, and therefore sync and fast sync, are unchanged.

Applies to tag beam-7.5.14493 (9c4366aae08e7fbde7bc8d65f828a0deace68bfc) with patch -p1.

